HST Office: registrymodifications.xcu survives a power cut and repairs itself.

- configmgr writemodfile.cxx TempFile::closeAndRename: fsync of the new file before the rename and of the
  user folder after it. Before, a power cut shortly after a write left the file with 0 bytes (XFS) and every
  setting and the recovery list were lost.
- configmgr components.cxx parseModificationLayer: a user registrymodifications.xcu that is empty or cannot
  be parsed is copied to registrymodifications.xcu.hong-<yyyymmdd-hhmmss>, replaced by the copy the office
  keeps in user/pack at every normal exit (or left to the defaults when there is none) and read again. A
  marker registrymodifications.xcu.hst-repaired ("restored" / "reset") makes the bundled extension tell the
  user at the next start (hst_office/profile_notice.py).
- desktop lockfile.cxx Lockfile::isStale: a profile lock a power cut left empty (it is written at start without
  fsync) names no other instance and is taken over, instead of asking "another instance is accessing your
  profile" before the recovery dialog (seen on XFS).
- comphelper BackupFileHelper::tryPopRegistryModifications: restores only registrymodifications from
  user/pack; the other profile parts the Safe Mode restore covers stay as they are.

